<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  {# Three layers, most immediate first:
     1. JS location.replace — instant, and keeps this page out of history so
        the back button doesn't bounce through the redirect.
     2. meta refresh — no-JS fallback.
     3. A visible link — in case both are disabled.
     Deliberately no <main class="page">: the SPA router treats a page without
     one as "not mine" and hands it to the browser, so the redirect always
     runs as a real navigation. #}
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ target }}">
  <script>location.replace("{{ target }}");</script>
</head>
<body>
  <p><a href="{{ target }}">Continue to the latest {{ kind }} →</a></p>
</body>
</html>
